From: Michal Szpakowski <michi.szpakowski@gmail.com>
Subject: [TEST v1] brcmfmac: pcie: reset the chip at hibernation power-off

Bisect step: MacBookPro13,1 powers itself off while restoring from a
hibernation image taken with brcmfmac loaded; the same image path
survives disk=test_resume (no power-off). The driver has no poweroff
callback, so the chip goes into the power-off with its firmware in the
D3-inform state. Reset it there, the same watchdog reset remove() does.

---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
@@ -2705,11 +2705,33 @@ cleanup:
 	return err;
 }
 
+static int brcmf_pcie_pm_poweroff(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct brcmf_pciedev_info *devinfo;
+	struct brcmf_bus *bus;
+
+	brcmf_dbg(PCIE, "Enter\n");
+
+	bus = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+	devinfo = bus->bus_priv.pcie->devinfo;
+
+	/*
+	 * The platform is about to lose power with the firmware still
+	 * running in its D3 state. Reset the chip first, as remove() does,
+	 * so that nothing is left running on it when the machine comes back.
+	 */
+	brcmf_err(bus, "hibernation power-off: resetting the chip\n");
+	brcmf_pcie_reset_device(devinfo);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static const struct dev_pm_ops brcmf_pciedrvr_pm = {
 	.suspend = brcmf_pcie_pm_enter_D3,
 	.resume = brcmf_pcie_pm_leave_D3,
 	.freeze = brcmf_pcie_pm_enter_D3,
 	.restore = brcmf_pcie_pm_leave_D3,
+	.poweroff = brcmf_pcie_pm_poweroff,
 };
 
 
